 First, we have the system of equations: \[
\begin{cases}
6x + 5y - 2z = -4 \\
4x + 5y + 12z = 54
\end{cases}
\] Subtracting the first equation from the second eliminates y: \[ (4x + 5y + 12z) - (6x + 5y - 2z) = 54 - (-4) \] This simplifies to: \[ -2x + 14z = 58 \] Or: \[ -x + 7z = 29 \] Solving for x: \[ x = 7z - 29 \] Substituting x into the first equation: \[ 6(7z - 29) + 5y - 2z = -4 \] This simplifies to: \[ 42z - 174 + 5y - 2z = -4 \] Or: \[ 40z + 5y = 170 \] Solving for y: \[ 5y = 170 - 40z \] \[ y = 34 - 8z \] Now we have x and y in terms of z: \[ x = 7z - 29 \] \[ y = 34 - 8z \] We want to find the value of \(x + y + z\): \[ x + y + z = (7z - 29) + (34 - 8z) + z = 7z - 29 + 34 - 8z + z = 5 \] So the value of \(x + y + z\) is: \[ \boxed{5} \] </think> <answer> 5 </answer>

